/**
 * A markdown table whose rows are prose, published as stacked blocks at every
 * width instead of as a table.
 *
 * WHAT IT IS FOR, measured over every English table of this site: in all but
 * one of them the longest column averages 126 characters a cell or fewer,
 * which is a clause, and a table is the right shape for it. In the exception,
 * the cost of a sweep (`api/cost.mdx`), the Notes column averages 281 characters
 * and runs to 1,259: paragraphs, one of them arguing why a family's figure
 * changed. A table is the right shape for numbers and the wrong one for an
 * argument, and that is true on a 1,280 px screen too, where the four data
 * columns render one line tall beside a note fifteen lines tall. The phone
 * only made it obvious: that page's table needed 674 px of horizontal scroll
 * inside a 328 px screen.
 *
 * So this is not a narrow-screen treatment. The breakpoints in
 * styles/tables.css already stack every table on a phone; this wraps the one
 * table that should never have been one, and it does it by declaring the same
 * ten `--table-*` properties with no query around them.
 *
 * WHY THE SOURCE STAYS A MARKDOWN TABLE. Three readers want this content and
 * only one of them is a browser: `docs/*.md` is generated from these pages by
 * scripts/gen-docs.mjs, and so are the markdown twin of the page and
 * llms-full.txt. A table is what a markdown reader can use, and a table is
 * what the author edits, so the rows are not moved into a data module and not
 * rewritten as a list. The reduction in src/lib/page-markdown.mjs unwraps this
 * component and leaves the table exactly as written, which is why turning this
 * page into a sheet changed no generated byte.
 *
 * The section HEADING stays in the markdown above this element rather than
 * being a prop: a heading emitted by a component is invisible to Starlight's
 * table of contents, which is built from the markdown AST, so moving it in
 * here would drop the section from "On this page" and lose its anchor.
 */
---

<div class="spec-sheet">
	<slot />
</div>
